From: BanaNAS <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] colors: BanaNAS palette

Match the black-bg splash image: pure black background bleeds into
the panel's natural off-state, banana-yellow progress fill on a
slightly lighter trough so the bar still reads at a glance, and
white text for the boot-stage messages.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [BanaNAS-specific branding override]

---
 psplash-colors.h | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/psplash-colors.h b/psplash-colors.h
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/psplash-colors.h
+++ b/psplash-colors.h
@@ -12,16 +12,16 @@
 #ifndef _HAVE_PSPLASH_COLORS_H
 #define _HAVE_PSPLASH_COLORS_H

-/* This is the overall background color */
-#define PSPLASH_BACKGROUND_COLOR 0xec,0xec,0xe1
+/* BanaNAS: pure black to match the splash image and panel off-state */
+#define PSPLASH_BACKGROUND_COLOR 0x00,0x00,0x00

-/* This is the color of any text output */
-#define PSPLASH_TEXT_COLOR 0x6d,0x6d,0x70
+/* White — readable on the black bg */
+#define PSPLASH_TEXT_COLOR 0xff,0xff,0xff

-/* This is the color of the progress bar indicator */
-#define PSPLASH_BAR_COLOR 0x6d,0x6d,0x70
+/* Banana yellow */
+#define PSPLASH_BAR_COLOR 0xf2,0xc0,0x35

-/* This is the color of the progress bar background */
-#define PSPLASH_BAR_BACKGROUND_COLOR 0xec,0xec,0xe1
+/* Bar trough — dark grey, just enough contrast against the bg */
+#define PSPLASH_BAR_BACKGROUND_COLOR 0x1a,0x1a,0x1a

 #endif
